{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_112","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'define \\\\(jolt-analyze-emit-form' host/chez/compile-eval.ss -A45; sed -n '235,280p' jolt-core/jolt/passes.clj\ntail -8 build/p1c-r3/stage1.log\"","aggregated_output":"523:(define (jolt-analyze-emit-form form ns)\n524-  (let* ((ctx (make-analyze-ctx ns))\n525-         ;; the form runs as soon as it compiles (hc-late-bound-namespace?)\n526-         (node (parameterize ((hc-compiling-to-run #t)) (jolt-ce-analyze ctx form))))\n527-    (jolt-lint-node! node)\n528-    (if (hc-compiler-direct-linking?)\n529-        (jolt-direct-link-emit node ctx)\n530-        (jolt-ce-emit (jolt-ce-run-passes node ctx)))))\n531-\n532-;; A form compiled under (binding [*compiler-options* {:direct-linking true}] ...)\n533-;; gets what `jolt build` gives every app form: calls to the vars defined this\n534-;; way bind their jv$ binding, small fns splice into their callers, and record\n535-;; and protocol types are inferred (#1377). It is the JVM's direct-linking\n536-;; contract: a caller compiled now keeps the body it saw when the callee is\n537-;; redefined later, and ^:dynamic / ^:redef opt a var out. Off that binding the\n538-;; spine stays open-world, exactly as before.\n539-;;\n540-;; The 3-arg run-passes takes the unit the back end emits with, which is the\n541-;; unit the passes' inline/record-shape state must land on (run-passes'\n542-;; invariant). The runtime spine's unit lives for the process, so the set of\n543-;; direct-linked defs accumulates across forms the way a build's does across\n544-;; namespaces.\n545-(define jolt-ce-current-unit (var-deref \"jolt.backend-scheme\" \"current-unit\"))\n546-(define (jolt-direct-link-emit node ctx)\n547-  (parameterize ((hc-form-direct-link #t))\n548-    (jolt-ce-emit (jolt-ce-run-passes node ctx (jolt-ce-current-unit)))))\n549-\n550-;; --- runtime defmacro -------------------------------------------------------\n551-;; Shared with